{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":448362,"name":"","username":"ThingsTinkerer","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/t/91b2a8/{size}.png","created_at":"2025-04-21T20:47:30.255Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eIf you don't need version control, I can understand that having all code in one file is easier. But node red already has the git integration in projects mode. Is there any good way of splitting flows.json into individual code files? Diffs are a pain and it would be a breeze to be able to synchronize particular flows or subflows across repos if having multiple files.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2025-04-22T06:10:30.239Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":27,"reads":28,"readers_count":27,"score":145.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":96692,"topic_slug":"split-flows-json-file-for-easier-diffs","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":27883,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/split-flows-json-file-for-easier-diffs/96692/1","calendar_details":[],"reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":448371,"name":"Stephen McLaughlin","username":"Steve-Mcl","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.nodered.org/steve-mcl/{size}/4826_2.png","created_at":"2025-04-22T06:09:38.824Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThis has been requested many times:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://discourse.nodered.org/t/formatted-function-node-with-separate-js-files/1760/2\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eFormatted Function Node with separate JS files - #2 by knolleary\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://discourse.nodered.org/t/flows-json-instead-of-flows-json/34043/6\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eFlows/*.json instead of flows.json? - #6 by knolleary\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://discourse.nodered.org/t/function-node-exported-json/77124/2\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eFunction Node exported json - #2 by knolleary\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne promising (and simple) solution would be to support YAML format (as Nick says in the first link) but unfortunately, as of writing, no one has picked this up.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAn option that would make diffs a \u003cem\u003elittle\u003c/em\u003e easier would be to enable the \u003ccode\u003eflowFilePretty\u003c/code\u003e flag in settings.js.   This will make JSON props much easier to compare (but function code will still be escaped unlike an equivalent YAML file format)\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2025-04-22T06:09:38.824Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":28,"readers_count":27,"score":20.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":96692,"topic_slug":"split-flows-json-file-for-easier-diffs","display_username":"Stephen McLaughlin","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://discourse.nodered.org/t/formatted-function-node-with-separate-js-files/1760/2","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Formatted Function Node with separate JS files","clicks":2},{"url":"https://discourse.nodered.org/t/flows-json-instead-of-flows-json/34043/6","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Flows/*.json instead of flows.json?","clicks":0},{"url":"https://discourse.nodered.org/t/function-node-exported-json/77124/2","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Function Node exported json","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":false,"staff":true,"user_id":1537,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/split-flows-json-file-for-easier-diffs/96692/2","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":448374,"name":"Gerrit Riessen","username":"gregorius","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.nodered.org/gregorius/{size}/73816_2.png","created_at":"2025-04-22T06:29:00.033Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI once created a visual comparison between a flow in the flow editor and the flow on the server --\u0026gt; \u003ca href=\"https://flows.nodered.org/node/@gregoriusrippenstein/node-red-contrib-flowcompare\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003enode-red-contrib-flowcompare (node) - Node-RED\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2025-04-22T06:29:00.033Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":27,"readers_count":26,"score":5.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":96692,"topic_slug":"split-flows-json-file-for-easier-diffs","display_username":"Gerrit Riessen","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://flows.nodered.org/node/@gregoriusrippenstein/node-red-contrib-flowcompare","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"node-red-contrib-flowcompare (node) - Node-RED","clicks":5}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":22947,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/split-flows-json-file-for-easier-diffs/96692/3","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":448394,"name":"","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.nodered.org/colin/{size}/17040_2.png","created_at":"2025-04-22T09:51:08.389Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThis doesn't help with diffing mods to the flow itself, but for mods within function nodes I use \u003ccode\u003eflowFilePretty\u003c/code\u003e and before committing to git I run a batch file containing:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003e#!/usr/bin/env sh\n\n# generates formatted versions of node red flow files matching flow*.json\n# in files flow*.json.formatted\n\n# NOTE must have flowFilePretty: true in settings.js\n\nfor f in *flow*.json; do\n  echo $f\n  sed -r 's/\\\\n/\\n/g' \"$f\" \u0026gt; \"$f.formatted\"\ndone\n# remove any cred files converted\nrm *_cred.json.formatted\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis escapes function nodes in flows files, generating \u003ccode\u003eflows.json.formatted\u003c/code\u003e files.  I include the formatted file in the git repo and a diff on that file shows the changes to the function nodes in an understandable format.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2025-04-22T09:51:08.389Z","reply_count":2,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":24,"readers_count":23,"score":19.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":96692,"topic_slug":"split-flows-json-file-for-easier-diffs","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":false,"staff":true,"user_id":65,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/split-flows-json-file-for-easier-diffs/96692/4","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":448432,"name":"","username":"ThingsTinkerer","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/t/91b2a8/{size}.png","created_at":"2025-04-22T12:07:13.281Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eSome nice workarounds and hacks, also found some interesting community packages that could help. But nothing would beat a native built-in solution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile I'm dreaming, first-class support for typescript? \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/joy.png?v=14\" title=\":joy:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":joy:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2025-04-22T12:07:13.281Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":4,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":23,"readers_count":22,"score":9.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":96692,"topic_slug":"split-flows-json-file-for-easier-diffs","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":65,"username":"Colin","name":"","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.nodered.org/colin/{size}/17040_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":27883,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/split-flows-json-file-for-easier-diffs/96692/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":448445,"name":"Gerrit Riessen","username":"gregorius","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.nodered.org/gregorius/{size}/73816_2.png","created_at":"2025-04-22T15:15:10.735Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Colin\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"96692\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex026/user_avatar/discourse.nodered.org/colin/48/17040_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Colin:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis doesn't help with diffing mods to the flow itself,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis the purpose of \u003ca href=\"http://flowhub.org\"\u003eflowhub.org\u003c/a\u003e - visual versioning of flows.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ThingsTinkerer\" data-post=\"5\" data-topic=\"96692\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/t/91b2a8/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e ThingsTinkerer:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut nothing would beat a native built-in solution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYep that's why there is a text-based, attribute by attribute diff built in to NodeRED.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2025-04-22T15:15:10.735Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":4,"quote_count":2,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":18,"readers_count":17,"score":8.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":96692,"topic_slug":"split-flows-json-file-for-easier-diffs","display_username":"Gerrit Riessen","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://flowhub.org","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"FlowHub.org","clicks":2}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":22947,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/split-flows-json-file-for-easier-diffs/96692/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":448457,"name":"","username":"ThingsTinkerer","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/t/91b2a8/{size}.png","created_at":"2025-04-22T17:31:10.179Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eIf flows.json was split, I could simply distribute a new version of a subflow by copying its file. At the moment distributing subflow version has become very difficult.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2025-04-22T17:31:10.179Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":16,"readers_count":15,"score":8.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":96692,"topic_slug":"split-flows-json-file-for-easier-diffs","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":22947,"username":"gregorius","name":"Gerrit Riessen","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.nodered.org/gregorius/{size}/73816_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":27883,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/split-flows-json-file-for-easier-diffs/96692/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":448459,"name":"Gerrit Riessen","username":"gregorius","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.nodered.org/gregorius/{size}/73816_2.png","created_at":"2025-04-22T17:41:03.529Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ThingsTinkerer\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"96692\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/t/91b2a8/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e ThingsTinkerer:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eparticular flows or subflows across repos if having multiple files.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ethat's what \u003ca href=\"http://flowhub.org\"\u003eflowhub.org\u003c/a\u003e does or helps with - since \u003ca href=\"http://flowhub.org\"\u003eflowhub.org\u003c/a\u003e works at the level of flow \u003cem\u003etabs\u003c/em\u003e not flows.json. So you create your flows.json using various flow tabs and each flow tab is hosted flowhub (i.e. in a github repo) and then you combine you individual flows into one large flows.json.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2025-04-22T17:41:03.529Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":16,"readers_count":15,"score":18.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":96692,"topic_slug":"split-flows-json-file-for-easier-diffs","display_username":"Gerrit Riessen","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://flowhub.org","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"FlowHub.org","clicks":8}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":22947,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/split-flows-json-file-for-easier-diffs/96692/8","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":455182,"name":"system","username":"system","avatar_template":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex026/uploads/nodered/original/1X/d073cd938eafa2e558d7c2cd59003b3ef4963033.png","created_